From c835ffa19689bfb9f1349fe1e3a33fe01967d0cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 06:37:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] system: say where the init could not keep an internal disk
 away

Where a disk that the list keeps away stayed attached (the kernel did not let
go of it, something was mounted from it), or where no disk could be kept
away because the disk of the system could not be told, nothing was said at
the start of Kodi, and the list said "In this start the internal disks are
hidden" where they were all attached. No internal partition is mounted in
such a start.

internal-disk-choice now says "this ... open", with the disks that stayed, or
"this ... unsafe". At the start of Kodi that is said first ("Not all disks
kept away: no internal partition is mounted", "No disk could be kept away:
no internal partition is mounted"), before a list that could not be read and
a kernel that could not hold the disks off. When the list is opened, a text
says which disks are still attached, that a program with full rights can
reach them in this start, that no partition of an internal disk is mounted in
it, where the kernel log has the details, and to restart the system to try
again; or why no disk was kept away. The offer to take a list that cannot be
read away says what goes while it cannot be read, and no longer that every
disk is kept away in this start. What keeping disks away means says this
case too.
---
